\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =\\frac{12}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}(\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{n}{[\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]}_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\pi }(-\\frac{\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )}{n}+\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =-\\frac{12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )}{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{n}=\\frac{12(-1)^{n+1}}{n}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379590 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379590 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379590 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379590 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379590 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379590 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379590 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186379593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379590 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "79a6378f-34e6-5fc5-aa94-a01fd4ad1963" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379591 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{12(1-(-1)^{n+1})}{\\pi n}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379591 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379591 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dbbdbe28-1ec6-5a1d-af09-19d933939c83" 